  {
   "index": 7,
   "tag": "p×2",
   "landmarks": [
    "main",
    "article"
   ],
   "textLength": 391,
   "text": "If you are looking for information about a specific author, try our About the Author page. Or, click the byline of the article you're reading.\nHowever, if your instructor requires you to use primary sources for your project, HowStuffWorks is not generally considered a primary source. The only exception would be articles, videos or podcasts in which we interview an expert about their work.",
